{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.121.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-119586-sqlite-libs",
              "name": "ApkMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119586 high vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite command-line shell through 3.54.1 contains a command injection vulnerability in the .recover command that emits attacker-planted dot-commands stored in sqlite_schema.sql values verbatim. Attackers can craft a database whose schema holds a valid CREATE statement followed by a .shell or .system line, executing OS commands when victims pipe .recover output into sqlite3."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119586",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-119586\nSeverity: high\nPackage: sqlite-libs\nVersion: 3.49.2-r1\nFix Version: \nType: apk\nLocation: /lib/apk/db/installed\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-119586](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119586)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-119586**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | sqlite-libs  | 3.49.2-r1  |   | apk  | /lib/apk/db/installed  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-119586](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119586)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:apk/alpine/sqlite-libs@3.49.2-r1?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=alpine-3.22.8\u0026upstream=sqlite"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-12781-python3",
              "name": "ApkMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-12781 medium vulnerability for python3 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When passing data to the b64decode(), standard_b64decode(), and urlsafe_b64decode() functions in the \"base64\" module the characters \"+/\" will always be accepted, regardless of the value of \"altchars\" parameter, typically used to establish an \"alternative base64 alphabet\" such as the URL safe alphabet. This behavior matches what is recommended in earlier base64 RFCs, but newer RFCs now recommend either dropping characters outside the specified base64 alphabet or raising an error. The old behavior has the possibility of causing data integrity issues.\n\n\n\n\nThis behavior can only be insecure if your application uses an alternate base64 alphabet (without \"+/\"). If your application does not use the \"altchars\" parameter or the urlsafe_b64decode() function, then your application does not use an alternative base64 alphabet.\n\n\n\n\nThe attached patches DOES NOT make the base64-decode behavior raise an error, as this would be a change in behavior and break existing programs. Instead, the patch deprecates the behavior which will be replaced with the newly recommended behavior in a future version of Python. Users are recommended to mitigate by verifying user-controlled inputs match the base64 \nalphabet they are expecting or verify that their application would not be \naffected if the b64decode() functions accepted \"+\" or \"/\" outside of altchars."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-12781",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-12781\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3\nVersion: 3.12.16-r0\nFix Version: \nType: apk\nLocation: /lib/apk/db/installed\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-12781](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-12781)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-12781**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | python3  | 3.12.16-r0  |   | apk  | /lib/apk/db/installed  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-12781](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-12781)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:apk/alpine/python3@3.12.16-r0?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=alpine-3.22.8"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-70873-sqlite-libs",
              "name": "ApkMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-70873 high vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An information disclosure issue in the zipfileInflate function in the zipfile extension in SQLite v3.51.1 and earlier allows attackers to obtain heap memory via supplying a crafted ZIP file."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-70873",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-70873\nSeverity: high\nPackage: sqlite-libs\nVersion: 3.49.2-r1\nFix Version: \nType: apk\nLocation: /lib/apk/db/installed\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-70873](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-70873)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-70873**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | sqlite-libs  | 3.49.2-r1  |   | apk  | /lib/apk/db/installed  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-70873](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-70873)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:apk/alpine/sqlite-libs@3.49.2-r1?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=alpine-3.22.8\u0026upstream=sqlite"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-4738-zlib",
              "name": "ApkMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-4738 critical vulnerability for zlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer vulnerability in OSGeo gdal (frmts/zlib/contrib/infback9 modules). This vulnerability is associated with program files inftree9.C‎.\n\nThis issue affects gdal: before 3.11.0."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security.alpinelinux.org/vuln/CVE-2026-4738",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-4738\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: zlib\nVersion: 1.3.2-r1\nFix Version: 1.4-r0\nType: apk\nLocation: /lib/apk/db/installed\nData Namespace: alpine:distro:alpine:3.22\nLink: [CVE-2026-4738](https://security.alpinelinux.org/vuln/CVE-2026-4738)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-4738**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | zlib  | 1.3.2-r1  | 1.4-r0  | apk  | /lib/apk/db/installed  | alpine:distro:alpine:3.22  | [CVE-2026-4738](https://security.alpinelinux.org/vuln/CVE-2026-4738)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:apk/alpine/zlib@1.3.2-r1?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=alpine-3.22.8"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-15366-python3",
              "name": "ApkMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-15366 medium vulnerability for python3 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The imaplib module, when passed a user-controlled command, can have additional commands injected using newlines. Mitigation rejects commands containing control characters."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-15366",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-15366\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: python3\nVersion: 3.12.16-r0\nFix Version: \nType: apk\nLocation: /lib/apk/db/installed\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-15366](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-15366)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-15366**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | python3  | 3.12.16-r0  |   | apk  | /lib/apk/db/installed  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-15366](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-15366)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:apk/alpine/python3@3.12.16-r0?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=alpine-3.22.8"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-119379-sqlite-libs",
              "name": "ApkMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119379 high vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite before 3.54.0 built with the session extension contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in sqlite3changeset_apply() that allows attackers to corrupt heap memory by supplying crafted changesets. Attackers can repeat a table name in a second changeset block with a larger column count, causing sessionUpdateFind() to memset past the undersized aUpdateMask allocation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119379",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-119379\nSeverity: high\nPackage: sqlite-libs\nVersion: 3.49.2-r1\nFix Version: \nType: apk\nLocation: /lib/apk/db/installed\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-119379](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119379)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-119379**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | sqlite-libs  | 3.49.2-r1  |   | apk  | /lib/apk/db/installed  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-119379](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119379)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:apk/alpine/sqlite-libs@3.49.2-r1?arch=x86_64\u0026distro=alpine-3.22.8\u0026upstream=sqlite"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-15367-python3",
              "name": "ApkMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-15367 medium vulnerability for python3 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The poplib module, when passed a user-controlled command, can have\nadditional commands injected using newlines. Mitigation rejects commands\ncontaining control characters."
