            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-119591-sqlite-libs",
              "name": "ApkMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-119591 medium vulnerability for sqlite-libs package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SQLite before 3.54.0 contains a stack exhaustion vulnerability in countOfViewOptimization() that allows attackers to crash the host process via count(*) over a large multi-row VALUES clause. Attackers supplying SQL or a database file with a crafted view can trigger deeply nested TK_PLUS expressions whose recursive freeing in sqlite3ExprDeleteNN() exhausts the C stack, causing denial of service."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119591",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-119591\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: sqlite-libs\nVersion: 3.49.2-r1\nFix Version: \nType: apk\nLocation: /lib/apk/db/installed\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-119591](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119591)",
